/*
 * Declares the MacroRuleSymbol class.
 *
 * A macro rule represents one of the grammar fragments used to decompose and
 * rewrite a macro expression during macro expansion. Unlike the constructor
 * rule, a macro rule is a secondary rewriting step, accessible either from the
 * macro constructor or from another macro rule.
 *
 * MacroRuleSymbol stores the syntactic rule and provides the symbolic identity
 * used during macro resolution.
 *
 * <hr>
 * 
 * @Package: ymirc        
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::symbol::macro_::rule
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/symbol/macro_/rule.yr
 * @Author(s):
